{
  "source": "Prompts/vector-space-v25.mp4",
  "duration": 201.216,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.0,
      "text": "Each AI token starts with a row of numbers called an embedding."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.44,
      "end": 6.02,
      "text": "As the AI processes your message,"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.5,
      "end": 9.52,
      "text": "its layers change those numbers to reflect the surrounding context."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.34,
      "end": 13.58,
      "text": "But those new numbers might not match the starting numbers for any token."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.4,
      "end": 15.74,
      "text": "How can they still represent meaning?"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.9,
      "end": 18.7,
      "text": "An exact match isn't necessary."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.42,
      "end": 21.24,
      "text": "The relationships between the numbers matter too."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.1,
      "end": 25.0,
      "text": "We can picture those relationships as positions on a map,"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.32,
      "end": 27.84,
      "text": "where nearby positions can represent similar meanings."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.66,
      "end": 30.5,
      "text": "That's the idea behind vector space."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.5,
      "end": 34.26,
      "text": "This map uses latitude and longitude to describe position."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.08,
      "end": 40.74,
      "text": "Let's add Dallas with its coordinates 32.78 degrees north, 96.80 degrees west."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.7,
      "end": 44.5,
      "text": "Next, add Mountain View, then New York City."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.4,
      "end": 48.16,
      "text": "Now you get coordinates that don't match one of our existing cities."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.96,
      "end": 52.22,
      "text": "The first is 38 degrees north, 120 degrees west."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.92,
      "end": 55.04,
      "text": "Mountain View is closest even without an exact match."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.78,
      "end": 59.22,
      "text": "Next, try 40 degrees north, 76 degrees west."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.74,
      "end": 61.5,
      "text": "New York City is closest to the second point."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.36,
      "end": 64.48,
      "text": "The coordinates didn't match either city exactly,"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.0,
      "end": 67.18,
      "text": "but distance helped us find the closest match."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.9,
      "end": 70.32,
      "text": "A map uses two numbers to describe a position,"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.84,
      "end": 72.84,
      "text": "but we can do the same with more than two numbers."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.64,
      "end": 76.58,
      "text": "Imagine a taste test, where you rate drinks on seven characteristics."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.8,
      "end": 79.1,
      "text": "We can't draw all seven dimensions,"
    },
    {
      "start": 79.3,
      "end": 82.02,
      "text": "but a simplified picture shows which drinks are closest."
    },
    {
      "start": 83.08,
      "end": 84.04,
      "text": "Let's add Coke to the map."
    },
    {
      "start": 84.68,
      "end": 85.36,
      "text": "Next is Pepsi."
    },
    {
      "start": 86.24,
      "end": 87.7,
      "text": "Pepsi's scores are close to Cokes,"
    },
    {
      "start": 88.22,
      "end": 90.5,
      "text": "so it sits near Coke in the soft drinks neighborhood."
    },
    {
      "start": 91.34,
      "end": 92.66,
      "text": "Now add a hot coffee."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.24,
      "end": 96.4,
      "text": "Hot coffee scores differ more from Cokes and Pepsi's,"
    },
    {
      "start": 96.44,
      "end": 98.94,
      "text": "so it sits farther away in the coffee and tea neighborhood."
    },
    {
      "start": 99.98,
      "end": 102.72,
      "text": "Now you get numbers that don't match any of our existing drinks."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.5,
      "end": 105.1,
      "text": "Let's add Mystery Drink A."
    },
    {
      "start": 105.8,
      "end": 107.94,
      "text": "Mystery Drink A is near Coke and Pepsi."
    },
    {
      "start": 108.58,
      "end": 109.82,
      "text": "It's first six numbers match both."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.62,
      "end": 112.06,
      "text": "Compare the last number, Citrus."
    },
    {
      "start": 112.62,
      "end": 116.74,
      "text": "Mystery Drink A is nine, Coke is one, and Pepsi is ten."
    },
    {
      "start": 117.28,
      "end": 117.9,
      "text": "Pepsi is closest."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.58,
      "end": 121.4,
      "text": "The Citrus Gap is only one, compared with eight for Coke."
    },
    {
      "start": 122.34,
      "end": 123.5,
      "text": "Now add Mystery Drink B."
    },
    {
      "start": 124.18,
      "end": 126.46,
      "text": "Mystery Drink B is in the coffee and tea neighborhood."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.18,
      "end": 129.26,
      "text": "Compare its seven numbers with hot coffees vector."
    },
    {
      "start": 129.92,
      "end": 131.82,
      "text": "Hot coffee is closest to Mystery Drink B."
    },
    {
      "start": 132.26,
      "end": 134.5,
      "text": "Its ratings are similar across all seven dimensions."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.5,
      "end": 138.28,
      "text": "Each drinks seven numbers give it a position in vector space."
    },
    {
      "start": 139.04,
      "end": 141.26,
      "text": "Comparing those numbers helps us find the closest match."
    },
    {
      "start": 141.81,
      "end": 143.32,
      "text": "This is the idea behind distance."
    },
    {
      "start": 143.92,
      "end": 145.64,
      "text": "Smaller gaps mean closer positions."
    },
    {
      "start": 146.5,
      "end": 149.08,
      "text": "AI uses this idea on a much larger scale."
    },
    {
      "start": 149.62,
      "end": 151.38,
      "text": "Its embeddings have thousands of dimensions,"
    },
    {
      "start": 151.82,
      "end": 153.28,
      "text": "with values learned during training."
    },
    {
      "start": 153.94,
      "end": 155.76,
      "text": "After the layers update a token's vector,"
    },
    {
      "start": 156.22,
      "end": 158.16,
      "text": "it doesn't need to match another vector exactly."
    },
    {
      "start": 159.08,
      "end": 161.56,
      "text": "Its position in vector space helps represent its meaning."
    },
    {
      "start": 162.34,
      "end": 165.9,
      "text": "Let's look at this meaning map to see how context changes position."
    },
    {
      "start": 166.62,
      "end": 167.7,
      "text": "Consider the sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 168.32,
      "end": 171.16,
      "text": "The tired cat sat on the mat during the May rainstorm."
    },
    {
      "start": 171.68,
      "end": 172.54,
      "text": "It soon fell asleep."
    },
    {
      "start": 173.58,
      "end": 176.02,
      "text": "On its own, it could refer to many things."
    },
    {
      "start": 176.86,
      "end": 178.54,
      "text": "As the layers process the sentence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 179.0,
      "end": 182.96,
      "text": "they update its numbers to carry information connecting it to cat."
    },
    {
      "start": 183.82,
      "end": 186.76,
      "text": "It remains a separate token, now near cat."
    },
    {
      "start": 187.68,
      "end": 190.98,
      "text": "Its new position reflects its connection to cat in this sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 191.96,
      "end": 193.94,
      "text": "Meaning is a position in vector space."
    },
    {
      "start": 195.08,
      "end": 196.7,
      "text": "Similar meanings usually sit close together."
    }
  ],
